00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:27.060
Sector rotation analysis identifies when capital shifts from one group of stocks to another even if the overall market is flat.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:34.780
Today's chip adjacent names all breaking out on the same day the broader market went nowhere shows how this works in practice.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:43.260
Investors can implement it by running a daily rotation view in a screener that flags sectors with above average relative strength and volume.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:48.860
The approach has historically worked best during periods when macro data creates uncertainty,

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:55.200
but specific industries still show independent confirmation. Risks include false signals when

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:01.160
volume lags or when a single headline reverses the flow. A concrete step is to load the five names

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:06.440
mentioned in the rotation report into a watch list and check their one month and six month trend

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:12.800
